      "message": "fix(post): retract Z before a later tool change's G49 (mazak, fanuc, doosan)\n\nEach section after the first wrote G49 and T M6 at the clearance height\nof the previous operation. The Mazak EIA/ISO manual says that G49 moves\nthe axis to remove the length offset, so Z could move down by the tool\nlength near the part. A FANUC-family control can do the same.\n\nThe Mazak, Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts now lift Z by the safeRetract\nmethod (G91 G28 Z0, or G53 G00 Z<safeRetractZ>) before the preamble's\nG90 ... G49 G80 block of each later section. A Go home or a setup-change\nlift that already raised Z is not repeated. On Fanuc and Doosan, a G43.4\nleft armed by a tilted section is cancelled (G49) before the lift, as\nGo home does, and the upright return no longer lifts a second time.\n\nGoldens moved: one \"G91 G28 Z0\" line before each later preamble in the\nmulti-tool Fanuc programs (three app goldens, eight catalog programs,\nexamples/first-part.nc). program_entry's z_homes no longer counts the\ntool-change lift as a trip home.\n\nFixes #4341\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
